{title: Breathe on Me, Breath of God}
{artist: Edwin Hatch & Robert Jackson}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 72}

Verse 1
[F]Breathe on me, [Bb]Breath of [F]God: fill [Bb]me with [F]life a[C]new,
that [F]I may [C]love what [Dm]thou dost [Bb]love, and [F]do what [C]thou wouldst [F]do.

Verse 2
[F]Breathe on me, [Bb]breath of [F]God, [Bb]Until my [F]heart is
pure, [F]Until with [C]Thee I [Dm]will [Bb]one will, [F]To do [C]and to [F]endure.

Verse 3
[F]Breathe on [Bb]me, breath [F]of God, [Bb]So [F]shall I
never [F]die, But [C]live [Dm]with Thee [Bb]the perfect [F]life [C]Of Thine [F]eternity.
